<div data-key="open" hidden>
<div style="text-align:center;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:26px;color:#8A5129">The key</p>
<h2 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:clamp(36px,3.8vw,56px);line-height:1.05">What your pictures might be telling you</h2>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">Read each one next to what you wrote down. These are signals, not verdicts. You're the only one who can tell which of them rings true.</p>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:22px;margin-top:40px">
<!-- the seven symbols in the game's order; English transcreation of the original Hungarian key (kincsesterkep.hu/megoldokulcs-kocka/), one of its sample answers each -->
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(-1deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 1</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The cube</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Your ego</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">How you really see yourself, what you think of yourself. How big was it? Did it fit in your palm (aren't you thinking a little small of yourself?), or was it the size of a house? What was it made of: light as a feather, moved by a breath of wind, or so heavy that several people could barely shift it? Was the surface smooth or scratched, did it carry any “injuries”? What colour was it, any decoration? Did it have a use, or was it just “pretty”? Did you like it, or was it simply there?</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “A battered old dice with deep scratches… well, yes, I've taken a few hits.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(0.8deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 2</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The ladder</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Your family and friends</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">One leg or two: does it stand on its own, or does it need something to lean on? What is it made of? Old or new, well used, in what condition? Would you happily climb it, sure that it would hold you? From here on, read every symbol this way: if this stands for the most important people in your life, what do you hold about them inside?</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “Lying on the ground, half buried in sand. I wonder what would happen if I dusted it off.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(-0.5deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 3</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The lion</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Problems that appear out of nowhere</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">And how you reacted says a lot. Did the cube come to mind first, or the ladder? Neither? Both? Would you fight, defend yourself or run? Do you recognise the way you handle problems in real life? Notice whether, by reflex, you listened to your ego or relied on the help of your family and friends.</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “I jumped into the cube and locked myself in.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(1.2deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 4</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The road</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Your path in life</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">The road is your life path, the way you see it ahead of you. Is it well trodden, do you know others have walked it before you? Is there traffic? Small, narrow and winding, or a huge motorway? Is it paved out in front of you, or just a tangle of footprints? How sure did it feel that it leads somewhere, and how much does that matter?</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “A dead-straight three-lane motorway, paved, painted, the works. A bit boring.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(-1.3deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 5</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The sea</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">How you feel right now</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">One of my favourites. The shore is a picture of your state of mind right now. What colour was the water, sky blue or grey? Clear or murky? Soft sand or sharp rocks? Friendly, or the kind that makes you shiver? Were there people, and how happily would you have stretched out there?</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “The waves were angry, all fizz and foam… and I loved it. It was alive!”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(0.6deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 6</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The house and the sign</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Your home, and a hidden message</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">The house is your home, the one you have now or your ideal one. Does it look lived in, or like an empty ghost house? Is it inviting, would you go in? Spick and span or ramshackle? A weekend cottage, or somewhere you'd settle? (People with a home of their own usually describe how they feel about it; people renting or in between describe the home they imagine.) The sign is a little trick: here your unconscious can leave you a message it thought important. If you saw nothing, that's fine.</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “I don't even need to go in. I know a family lives there, the fire is lit, and the rooms are kind.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
<article style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(20,34,48,.12);padding:26px 24px;border-radius:4px;transform:rotate(-0.8deg)">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129">No. 7</p>
<h3 class="display" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:28px">The horse</h3>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:21px;color:#1C4F6B">Your relationship</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">The last one branches two ways too: your current partner, or your ideal one, comes to you as the horse. How does it behave with you? What does it look like, what is it doing? Is it free or tethered? How do you approach each other: are you in tune straight away, or does it take a long time to win its trust? (If you're in a relationship, it's often your partner; if you're on your own, it shows the picture you hold of the next one.)</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;font-style:italic;color:#4A5560">Someone wrote: “A beautiful, free stallion… I know it won't be easy to win him over, but if it happens… oh.”</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#1C4F6B;border-bottom:1px dashed #B9C9D6;padding-bottom:4px">My picture:</p>
</article>
</div>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:#4A5560;text-align:center">[English transcreation of the original Hungarian key, Sophie to check]</p>
<p class="display" style="margin:46px auto 0;max-width:640px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(26px,2.6vw,34px);font-style:italic;color:#1C4F6B;line-height:1.25">What surprised you most? Write it down in one sentence. That's your first bearing.</p>
</div>
</section>

